        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2006",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x - 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = 2$: $A = -2$, $B = 1$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{-2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x - 2}$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
